Build a universal, configurable sports scoring app using Flutter.

The app will let users:

Select a sport and match format.

Add individual players or teams of any supported size.

Track scores, servers, receivers, and serving positions.

Assign matches to specific courts.

Run multiple matches independently.

Save match history and results offline.

Primary goals

Flexible player configuration: Support singles, doubles, triples, team-based sports, and configurable formats where permitted.

Sport-specific scoring: Automatically calculate points, games, sets, winning conditions, and serving rotations.

Accurate service tracking: Identify the serving player, receiving player, serving side, and service court whenever the sport requires them.

Court management: Organize active matches by court.

Offline-first operation: Keep scoring available without internet access.

Expandable architecture: Make it straightforward to add new sports and rule variations.